    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d733">

                <pb facs="0576" n="494" xml:id="pg494"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/1962.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-05-26"><hi rendition="#italic">May 26,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>At 3.30 o’clock, of May 25, 1911, the President and Vice President resigned and
                    Provisional President de la Barra issued a proclamation to the Mexican people.
                    President Diaz left for Vera Cruz at 4.15 o’clock on the-morning of May 26 on an
                    armed train; he will sail for Europe. Nearly all the Científicos have left or
                    are now leaving the country. Everything was quiet in the city. In the Chamber of
                    Deputies, where Mr. de la Barra took the oath of office in the presence of the
                    diplomatic corps, perfect order was maintained.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
